<!-- ════════════ HEADER ════════════ -->
<div class="report-header">
  <div class="container" style="padding-top:0;padding-bottom:0;">
    <div class="label">Strategic Intelligence Briefing &nbsp;·&nbsp; Research Policy Analysis</div>
    <h1>Biomedical Research Landscape 2024–2026</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Publication Trends, Topic Dynamics, and Open Access Patterns across 4,886 PubMed-indexed abstracts — a representative sample drawn from the full 126,832-record dataset.</p>
    <div class="report-meta">
      <span><strong>Dataset:</strong> PubMed Biomedical Abstracts 2024–2026</span>
      <span><strong>Records Analyzed:</strong> 4,886</span>
      <span><strong>Coverage:</strong> January 2024 – March 2026</span>
      <span><strong>Generated:</strong> April 21, 2026</span>
      <span><strong>Audience:</strong> Research Policy Analysts &amp; Funding Strategists</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="container">

<!-- ════════════ TOC ════════════ -->
<div class="toc">
  <h2>Table of Contents</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><a href="#kpis">Key Performance Indicators</a></li>
    <li><a href="#publication-volume">Publication Volume &amp; Temporal Distribution</a></li>
    <li><a href="#geographic">Geographic Landscape</a></li>
    <li><a href="#topics">Research Topic &amp; MeSH Analysis</a></li>
    <li><a href="#open-access">Open Access Adoption &amp; Journals</a></li>
    <li><a href="#research-type">Research Type &amp; Collaboration</a></li>
    <li><a href="#takeaways">Key Takeaways &amp; Strategic Implications</a></li>
  </ol>
</div>

<!-- ════════════ KPIs ════════════ -->
<div id="kpis" class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="section-num">Dashboard</div>
    <h2>Key Performance Indicators</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="kpi-grid">
    <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color:#2e86ab;">
      <div class="kpi-label">Total Records</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">4,886</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Sample from 126,832-record corpus</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color:#3bb273;">
      <div class="kpi-label">Overall Open Access Rate</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">65.2%</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">3,183 of 4,886 articles</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color:#9333ea;">
      <div class="kpi-label">Median Authors / Article</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">6</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Mean: 7.1 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Max: 115</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color:#f4a261;">
      <div class="kpi-label">Top 10 Countries Share</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">50.0%</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">2,444 of 4,886 records (normalized)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color:#e84855;">
      <div class="kpi-label">MeSH Coverage</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">52.9%</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">2,583 records with major_topic</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color:#1a3a5c;">
      <div class="kpi-label">Median Abstract Length</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">223</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Words per abstract (mean: 224)</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ════════════ SECTION 1 — PUBLICATION VOLUME ════════════ -->
<div id="publication-volume" class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="section-num">Section 01</div>
    <h2>Publication Volume &amp; Temporal Distribution</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="data-note">
    <strong>Indexing Lag Advisory:</strong> Approximately 80% of records are dated 2024, consistent with the well-documented PubMed indexing lag — older publications accumulate more indexed entries over time. 2025 and 2026 figures represent <em>in-progress</em> indexing and should not be interpreted as declining output. The January 2024 spike (1,665 records) reflects bulk backfill indexing rather than a true publication surge.
  </div>

  <div class="kpi-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);margin-top:8px;">
    <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color:#2e86ab;">
      <div class="kpi-label">2024 Publications</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">3,924</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">80.3% of dataset</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color:#f4a261;">
      <div class="kpi-label">2025 Publications</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">737</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">15.1% of dataset (indexing ongoing)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card" style="--kpi-color:#3bb273;">
      <div class="kpi-label">2026 Publications</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">225</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">4.6% — Jan–Mar only</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-card">
    <h3>Monthly Publication Volume — Known-Month Records</h3>
    <p class="chart-desc">Records with explicit pub_month only (excludes 14.7% of 2024 records and 24.3% of 2025 records flagged "Unknown"). Jan 2024 bulk-indexing spike is a data artifact.</p>
    <div class="chart-wrap chart-wrap-tall">
      <canvas id="chartMonthly"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="two-col">
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h3>Year-over-Year Volume</h3>
      <p class="chart-desc">Raw record counts by publication year. 2026 covers only Q1.</p>
      <div class="chart-wrap chart-wrap-med">
        <canvas id="chartYearVol"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h3>2025 Monthly Trend (excl. Unknown)</h3>
      <p class="chart-desc">Monthly rhythm in 2025, showing a Dec-2025 uptick (94 records) consistent with year-end indexing runs.</p>
      <div class="chart-wrap chart-wrap-med">
        <canvas id="chart2025Monthly"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Interpretation Note</strong>
    The 2025 monthly series (Jan–Dec) shows a relatively flat 30–56 record range from Jan–Nov, with a notable uptick in December (94). The 2026 trajectory (51 → 76 → 98 from Jan to Mar) is the <em>most reliable growth signal</em> in the dataset since these records have had the least time to accumulate indexing lag.
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ════════════ SECTION 2 — GEOGRAPHIC ════════════ -->
<div id="geographic" class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="section-num">Section 02</div>
    <h2>Geographic Landscape of Biomedical Research</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="callout success">
    <strong>Key Finding</strong>
    China and the United States together account for 31.7% of all records (China: 21.0%; US: 10.7%), with the next eight countries each contributing under 5%. The research landscape is highly concentrated at the top but broadly distributed across 80+ countries.
